# This site is exported as a static build (GitHub Pages), so live data is
# fetched from the BROWSER via public, keyless (or key-but-not-secret) APIs.
# Copy this file to `.env.local` — values are inlined into the client bundle.
#
# All vars are optional: an unset widget renders a styled "demo" state.

# AWS / Vercel style: only `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` vars are exposed to the browser.
# Only ever put PUBLIC values here. NEVER put real secrets (e.g. a Spotify
# client secret or refresh token) in a static export — they can't be hidden.

# Discord presence (Lanyard) — keyless, needs only your NUMERIC user ID.
# Right-click your avatar > Copy User ID (enable Developer Mode in Discord).
# Make sure your Discord account is registered with Lanyard: https://lanyard.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_DISCORD_USER_ID=

# Last.fm — app-scoped public key (a key, NOT a secret). Optional.
# Create one at https://www.last.fm/api/account/create
NEXT_PUBLIC_LASTFM_API_KEY=

# GitHub profile — no key needed at all (public REST API). This is optional only
# if you want to hardcode a different handle than pedro3pv.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GITHUB_USER=pedro3pv
